&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Platform Engineer to help build, operate, and improve the software delivery and developer infrastructure platforms used by engineering teams working on large-scale C++ and Python applications. This role combines platform engineering, CI/CD, build systems, infrastructure automation, observability, artifact management, and developer productivity. The ideal candidate has strong systems engineering fundamentals and practical experience supporting complex engineering workflows in a production-critical environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, and enhancing tools that support developer productivity, systems infrastructure, and DevOps practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the global Platform, Developer Infrastructure, and Release Engineering team to align regional solutions with global standards while representing local engineering, operational, and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve build and release infrastructure for large-scale C++ and Python applications, including build tooling, dependency management, CI/CD integration, artifact workflows, and developer self-service capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with software engineers, infrastructure engineers, quants, traders, and SRE teams to design, build, and operate reliable software delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and operate scalable CI/CD pipelines for build, test, artifact promotion, deployment, and release workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain infrastructure automation and configuration management solutions for platform, CI/CD, artifact, and developer infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop internal developer tooling and self-service platform capabilities that reduce operational toil and improve developer productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use containerization and orchestration technologies to support reproducible builds, reliable CI/CD execution, and consistent deployment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve observability for build, CI/CD, release, and platform services through centralized logging, metrics, tracing, dashboards, and alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and optimize build, CI/CD, artifact, and developer infrastructure systems with a focus on performance, reliability, scalability, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement software supply chain security practices, including artifact provenance, dependency management, vulnerability scanning, secret management, and CI/CD security controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in incident response, root cause analysis, and continuous improvement for platform-owned build, release, CI/CD, and developer infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and recommend improvements to build, release, CI/CD, developer infrastructure, observability, and software delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of hands-on engineering experience building, operating, or improving software delivery, platform, infrastructure, CI/CD, DevOps, SRE, or developer productivity systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux systems knowledge and troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software build systems, especially for large C++ codebases; experience with CMake, Ninja, Bazel, Buck2, or similar tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python packaging, dependency management, and environment management tools such as pip, conda, uv, pixi, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating CI/CD platforms, including pipeline design, build/test automation, artifact promotion, secrets handling, and failure diagnosis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with artifact repositories, binary/package distribution, and artifact lifecycle management using tools such as Artifactory, Nexus, Harbor, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure automation and configuration management tools such as Terraform, Ansible, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerization technologies such as Docker or Podman; familiarity with orchestration platforms such as Kubernetes, Nomad, ECS, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud, hybrid, or on-premises infrastructure environments; AWS, GCP, Azure, or private infrastructure experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and shell scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Git and collaborative development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of networking fundamentals, including DNS, load balancing, TLS, HTTP, routing, and service discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of distributed systems reliability concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience gathering developer feedback and translating recurring pain points into self-service tooling, automation, documentation, or platform improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to work in a fast-paced, globally distributed engineering environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience with:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting C++ build, linkage, dependency, ABI, compiler, linker, and toolchain issues in large codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernizing legacy build systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving build reproducibility, reducing build times, or introducing remote caching / remote execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing reproducible Python environments and internal package distribution workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability platforms such as Prometheus, Grafana, OpenTelemetry, OpenSearch, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow orchestration technologies such as Airflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GitOps deployment methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building internal developer portals, self-service workflows, or paved-road developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems programming languages such as C++ and/or Rust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software supply chain security practices such as dependency provenance, vulnerability scanning, and secret management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrating AI-assisted development tools into engineering workflows while maintaining appropriate security, access control, and code review practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anticipated New York annual base salary range $150,000 - $200,000, plus eligible for discretionary bonus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

ed99f834674a2ef8bf355ae1e98dabf2fcb316ba:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Fixed Income &amp;amp; Macro, Event &amp;amp; Multi-Asset RV, Equity L/S &amp;amp; Capital Markets, and Quantitative Trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Technology and Strats (Quant) teams build and operate the engineering platform behind the firm&#39;s investment activity and business functions globally. Working alongside the investment teams to create edge in research, portfolio construction, execution and risk management, and applying machine learning and AI across both the investment process and the firm&#39;s platform operations. Strategic Analytics (&quot;Strats&quot;), with its quantitative researchers and developers, partner directly with Portfolio Managers and the businesses on strategy-specific research, models, signals, backtesting and execution, while building the shared pricing, analytics and research infrastructure used across strategies. The core Technology teams own the firm&#39;s market, reference and alternative data platform; the infrastructure including cloud, compute, developer tooling, security and connectivity that everything at the firm runs on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Linux Engineering owns the platform that most of Verition&#39;s compute runs on. This is deep, hands-on infrastructure work: the Linux fleet across our private data centers and cloud regions, tuned for the performance and latency demands of a quantitative trading firm, and automated so that thousands of machines behave as one coherent, code-defined platform. As a Senior Platform Engineer, you&#39;ll own significant pieces of that surface directly — from kernel-level tuning on our most latency-sensitive systems to the automation that provisions and maintains the fleet — working closely with the Tech Lead for Linux Platform Engineering to execute one coherent OS-platform strategy, alongside the Windows Engineering team that owns its counterpart.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer, automate, and operate the firm&#39;s Linux fleet across private data centers and cloud regions, holding it to the reliability, performance, and security standards demanded by a quantitative trading environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform kernel-level and system-level performance tuning on latency-sensitive systems, including core pinning and shielding, kernel bypass, network stack tuning, and interrupt steering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain deployment, configuration, patching, and monitoring automation in Python and modern configuration management, treating the Linux estate as code rather than as hand-managed servers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own significant pieces of the Linux platform surface hands-on across both Red Hat Enterprise Linux and Ubuntu, from provisioning through in-life management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce Linux security baselines and hardening standards, partnering with Security Engineering on patching cadence, privileged access, and the firm&#39;s broader identity and short-lived-credential strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the OS-platform technical strategy set by the Tech Lead, Linux Platform Engineering, bringing deep Linux expertise so that decisions span both platforms coherently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Data Center &amp;amp; Fleet Infrastructure on provisioning and asset management, and with Developer Tools &amp;amp; Infrastructure on build and CI integration, so the Linux platform is well-integrated with the rest of the stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide production support for the Linux surface, including participation in an on-call rotation, and drive continuous improvement of its reliability and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers across the team on Linux internals, performance, and automation, raising the bar for how the firm builds and operates Linux infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience in systems or platform engineering, with a focus on Linux infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience with the inner workings of the Linux kernel, including core pinning and shielding, kernel bypass, network stack tuning, and interrupt steering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of both Red Hat Enterprise Linux and Ubuntu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience automating deployment, configuration, patching, and monitoring with Python, including modern configuration-management approaches (e.g., Ansible, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and applying Linux security baselines and hardening standards (e.g., CIS Benchmarks, STIGs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed systems and cloud platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree or PhD in Engineering, Computer Science, or related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in one or more general-purpose programming languages (e.g., C++, Java, Rust).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with “metal as a service” type build factories and Kubernetes-based bare-metal provisioning systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience tuning Linux for low-latency or trading-adjacent workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of agentic developer productivity tooling and customization such as spec-driven development, MCP servers, and Claude Code sub-agents, skills, and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 years of experience working in a complex, matrixed organization involving cross-functional or cross-business projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with quantitative developers and researchers in a finance setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to relevant open-source projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary range for this position is $150,000 to $200,000 (USD). In addition to base salary, this position is eligible for a discretionary performance bonus and a comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as geographic location, work experience, qualifications, and skill level.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

77f7baa583576d6c08bb49537cc3c42aba94b97c:
&lt;p&gt;Squarepoint is looking for a Junior Desktop Support Analyst to support a global community of approximately 2000+ users in a Windows environment consisting of virtual desktops. Candidate will interact onsite and remotely with users to provide support with workstation applications such as Microsoft Office, Access Management via Windows Active Directory, Remote Access assistance and hardware issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver 24x5 on-site and remote support to approximately 2,000 global users in accordance with business requirements;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in a rotational on-call schedule to provide weekend support;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage service requests and incidents within defined service-level agreements, in line with documented internal runbooks;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide first- and second-level support by triaging, diagnosing, and resolving service issues;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Level 2 and Level 3 internal teams, external partners, and vendors to resolve complex incidents;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide end-to-end hardware support, including inventory management and equipment procurement as required;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain knowledge base articles and runbooks related to support processes, system changes, and operating procedures;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure effective execution of the Incident Management process to minimize production impact on end users;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide project support to senior team members as required;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience in a Microsoft environment supporting Windows 11, Office Suite including Office 365, and Azure, including SharePoint;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience with Active Directory, Remote Access solutions;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience installing, troubleshooting, and managing desktop hardware;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dedication to customer service;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works with minimum supervision, proactively follow up on outstanding issues/tickets;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle multiple tasks with changing priorities and capable to handle frequent interruptions positively;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, prioritizing, interpersonal, problem-solving skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated collaborative skills and ability to work well within a team;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced and deadline-oriented environment;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with critical attention to detail, deadlines, and reporting;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Engineering or related field or experience;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting in PowerShell and Python to proactively automate common tasks to improve efficiency and increase productivity;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software packaging and deployment;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage small-medium sized projects within defined timeline and budget;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in learning about new and emerging technologies;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed learner and ability to find solutions to problems they have not encountered before&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

dc314b764c4bc50b9c1638fa549f9c086f2778ed:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
