&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AHL fosters a performance driven, meritocratic culture with a small company, no-attitude feel. It is flat structured, open, transparent, and collaborative, offering ample opportunity to grow and have enormous impact on what we do. &amp;nbsp;We are actively engaged with the broader research and academic community, as well as renowned industry contributors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a596af68d69b4f637f3d28abad5c06593972cffa:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Fixed Income &amp;amp; Macro, Event &amp;amp; Multi-Asset RV, Equity L/S &amp;amp; Capital Markets, and Quantitative Trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Technology and Strats (Quant) teams build and operate the engineering platform behind the firm&#39;s investment activity and business functions globally. Working alongside the investment teams to create edge in research, portfolio construction, execution and risk management, and applying machine learning and AI across both the investment process and the firm&#39;s platform operations. Strategic Analytics (&quot;Strats&quot;), with its quantitative researchers and developers, partner directly with Portfolio Managers and the businesses on strategy-specific research, models, signals, backtesting and execution, while building the shared pricing, analytics and research infrastructure used across strategies. The core Technology teams own the firm&#39;s market, reference and alternative data platform; the infrastructure including cloud, compute, developer tooling, security and connectivity that everything at the firm runs on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platform Services builds and supports the business tools the firm uses day to day such as web applications, reporting and workflow tools, the data that sits behind them, and an emerging layer of AI-assisted tooling. It is a small team working close to its users, and it owns what it builds end to end. You will work alongside experienced engineers on live, in-use applications: building features, improving the data underneath them, supporting the people who rely on them, and strengthening the development and release practices around them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is deliberately broad. In each week you might write a query, ship a front-end change, debug a deployment, and talk a colleague through a problem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain features across a suite of internal web applications used across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver the steady stream of small, high-visibility requests: new fields, layout and usability improvements, filtering, export and upload handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve query and page performance on tools that are used daily.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and tune SQL to answer business questions and diagnose issues in operational and reference data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve data-quality problems — malformed values, mismatched identifiers, records failing validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the flows that move data between internal systems, and help build the derived or historical datasets that source systems do not retain themselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the integration layer that connects internal systems to LLM-based tooling — building and testing tool interfaces, improving error handling, and extending logging and administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal AI assistant features through functional testing, access-control testing, and triage of reported behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package and document tooling so non-technical colleagues can use it without hands-on help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as first-line support for internal users — access requests, permissions, and environment or configuration problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle account and role provisioning and the associated directory group changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own routine operational tasks: deployments, scheduled restarts, cache management, and monitoring of automated jobs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep runbooks, release notes, and status updates current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help mature the codebase — source control conventions, branching, code review, and continuous integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up development environments so changes can be tested properly before release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add automated testing, starting with the paths that break most often.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year of experience in a similar position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills and comfortable working in a web application codebase (HTML/CSS/JavaScript).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Python — joins, aggregation, window functions, reading an execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take a vague request to a working, deployed result without being managed through every step.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain a technical constraint in plain language, and follow up without being chased.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to financial services is preferred — trade lifecycle, securities reference data, or fund and portfolio structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Docker, Linux, and cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with LLM tooling — agent frameworks, tool-calling integrations, or building against an LLM API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with issue tracking and documentation tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary range for this position is $100,000 to $150,000 (USD). In addition to base salary, this position is eligible for a discretionary performance bonus and a comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate will be determined based on a variety of factors such as geographic location, work experience, qualifications, and skill level.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$100,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

f694e8be895171b921b05dbe1396e8166d5095c3:
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is a leading quantitative trading firm founded in 1998. Tower has built its business on a high-performance platform and independent trading teams. We have a 25+ year track record of innovation and a reputation for discovering unique market opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note, this internship opportunity is open to those who are available from February 2027 for six months.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Iterating quickly with on-site quantitative researchers on the research processes in order to improve the desk&#39;s quantitative trading strategies P&amp;amp;L&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing Python tools used in trading strategies research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the existing simulation/backtest framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help global research team on EMEA-related research through various communication channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently in the final year of a Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Applied Math, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in quantitative finance and software development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid foundation in Python programming and exposure to libraries such as NumPy, Pandas, or Polars through coursework or personal projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated curiosity, problem-solving ability, and a desire to grow in a fast-paced, collaborative, and intellectually demanding environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication skills and willingness to work as part of a distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to C++ and/or scripting languages (e.g., Bash) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in learning about large-scale systems, workflow orchestration, and production-grade software engineering practices&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exciting networking and social events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to learn from senior management across the firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentors from your alma mater and other top institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

