b204b55c1388964e90c7846b255c03596fc2188e:
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is a leading quantitative trading firm founded in 1998. Tower has built its business on a high-performance platform and independent trading teams. We have a 25+ year track record of innovation and a reputation&amp;nbsp; for discovering unique market opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with quantitative traders and software developers to operate and supervise our automated trading strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring production trading for risk and compliance issues and quickly responding to unusual behaviors or market conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively troubleshooting and resolving issues related to day-to-day trading activities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing programming scripts and applications to automate and facilitating our trading system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzing production trades and market data, and developing ideas to improve our trading strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working a late evening schedule to provide trading and production support aligned with relevant market hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in a technical or quantitative field, such as computer science, engineering, mathematics, physics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a trade monitoring, trading, or trade support role is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to analyze trading data, investigate issues, and draw actionable conclusions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of futures markets, including products, trading venues, market structure, and risk management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of algorithmic trading technology and architecture, including UNIX/Linux environments and monitoring applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python to support existing infrastructure and identify areas for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively on complex tasks, take initiative, and assume increasing responsibility over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and fluency in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anticipated New York annual base salary range $120,000- $200,000, plus eligible for bonus(es).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

45eb3c3b5a3b30e495cfa9321655037c4b85e09f:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is looking for a Junior Trading Ops/DevOps Engineer to join our growing team in Chicago. You&#39;d work within&amp;nbsp;the technology landscape safeguarding the performance and stability of proprietary trading systems and related&amp;nbsp;hardware, with direct ownership of technical issues in in-house trading applications. The role blends SRE, Operations&amp;nbsp;Engineer, and DevOps Engineer responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Deploy, run, and monitor production latency-sensitive trading applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Automate trading infrastructure/application management in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Triage and resolve live incidents in a fast-paced trading environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Create and integrate monitoring and alerting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Work with Linux, network, and datacenter engineers to troubleshoot issues and optimize trading performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Assist with rollout of new products, systems, and exchanges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Conduct user acceptance testing across internal trading application stacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Review incidents for recurring themes and feed technical requirements back into the development cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, or a related Engineering/Science discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-2 years of relevant work experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming ability&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High proficiency in Python on Linux Platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Networking knowledge/interest is a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting instincts and root-cause discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and eagerness to learn how systems fit together&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work under pressure and with frequent interruption&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong teamwork and collaboration ability&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid Medical, Dental, Vision, Disability, and Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully stocked kitchen; free breakfast and lunch every day on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Vacation, Sick, and Parental leaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter and Flexible Spending Programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In office M-F with 10 remote days per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$150,000 - $200,000 - Salaries are based on numerous factors such as skills, experience, and education. Our compensation package also includes a discretionary bonus and a comprehensive benefits program for full-time employees. For more information, reach out to your recruiter.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Old Mission is not accepting unsolicited resumes from any staffing/search firms. All resumes submitted by staffing/search firms to any employee at Old Mission via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid signed search agreement will be deemed the sole property of Old Mission, and no fee will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Old Mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

5bc8c4ea279f8255f7dac9ce1f9cfa0791dab8e2:
Are you ready for two days on a real trading floor? 
 Join the Flow Quant Trading Days at our Amsterdam office on 7 &amp; 8 December 2026 - a hands-on quant trading academy for a select group of 15 students. Find out whether trading is for you with an exciting look inside our Trading floor, and the chance to receive a full-time job offer as a Graduate Trader.
 Over two days you'll price, arbitrage and hedge in live simulations, make markets under real time pressure, and go head-to-head with our traders in games built to test your instinct. You will have the opportunity to show your curiosity while shadowing the trading desks, watching news as it hits the market.
 What's in it for you? 
 An insight into trading at Flow Traders; 
 Introductory classes on traditional finance, Crypto and ETFs; 
 Hands-on simulations where you can show your competitive spirit; 
 Desk shadowing in small groups; 
 Games night to demonstrate your trading intuition - where you’ll go head-to-head with our traders; 
 Our in-house facilities: gym with personal trainers, bar, barista, arcade room, and a lounge with daily catered lunches from our chef; 
 Dinner in Amsterdam and farewell drinks in the Flow Bar with the trading team; 
 And of course, the chance to receive a full-time job offer as a Graduate Trader. 
 Do you have what it takes? 
 Are you graduating in 2026 or 2027 from a BSc/MSc STEM degree in the Netherlands, with a demonstrable interest in trading on your CV? Do you code - Python or otherwise - and enjoy reasoning with probabilities and brainteasers? Can you spot an opportunity, and are you assertive enough to seize it? We're looking for competitive, curious and entrepreneurial students.
 The application procedure 
 We invite you to apply through our website by submitting your resume as well as a persuasive cover letter. The application deadline will be November 13 th . 
 Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.

dfeaf2d2-75ed-4282-8a63-3fdfb8daca41:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acadian Asset Management is a global, systematic investment manager at the forefront of data-driven investing since 1986. Headquartered in Boston, with locations in Singapore, London, and Sydney, we manage over $232 billion on behalf of leading institutions worldwide—including pension funds, endowments, foundations, and sovereign wealth funds. We harness advanced technology, rich datasets, and multidisciplinary expertise to help clients navigate complex markets and uncover insights that may be overlooked by traditional approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What sets Acadian apart is our people. We foster a collaborative, intellectually curious environment where ideas are tested, diverse perspectives are welcomed, and innovation thrives. We’re united by a shared purpose: delivering effective client outcomes and supporting one another in work that’s both challenging and rewarding. We offer a flexible hybrid work environment, strong benefits, and a casual but focused office culture—all designed to support the meaningful, collaborative work that defines Acadian.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner with the Performance Attribution Group (PAG) and Investment Operations to solve complex business problems and shape the technology that supports one of the firm&#39;s core investment capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced Business Systems Architect who combines strong technology and analytical skills with a &lt;strong&gt;deep understanding of Performance &amp;amp; Attribution, Securities Operations, or related investment operations disciplines&lt;/strong&gt;. You should be comfortable working with the data and workflows behind portfolio performance—from securities, transactions, positions, pricing, and benchmarks through performance calculation, attribution, and downstream reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who is motivated by solving business problems—not just gathering requirements.&lt;/strong&gt; Success in this role comes from curiosity, sound judgment, and a genuine desire to understand how the business works before designing practical technology solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, on-site position based in Boston, Massachusetts. Acadian supports a hybrid work environment; employees are on-site in the Boston office 3 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships across the Performance Attribution Group (PAG), Investment Operations, Client Reporting, Enterprise Technology, and strategic technology vendors to drive successful business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead analysis from concept through implementation, translating business needs into practical technology solutions that deliver measurable value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze complex investment workflows, data, and business processes to identify opportunities to improve efficiency, data quality, and operational resiliency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate business and data issues across systems, identify root causes, and partner with business and technology teams to implement sustainable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the future of Acadian&#39;s Performance &amp;amp; Attribution technology capabilities by aligning technology with evolving business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with software engineers, architects, and technology vendors to deliver scalable, high-quality technology solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously explore emerging technologies and better ways of working. We value curiosity, thoughtful experimentation, and continuous learning in pursuit of better business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor teammates, share knowledge, and bring structure and clarity to complex business and technology challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Looking for Teammates With:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of Business Systems Analysis experience supporting technology within the investment management industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience supporting Performance &amp;amp; Attribution, Securities Operations, Investment Operations, Portfolio Accounting, or related investment management functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success building trusted partnerships with business stakeholders and delivering technology solutions that solve complex business problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading business analysis throughout the software delivery lifecycle within an Agile environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding analytical, facilitation, communication, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with investment management platforms and enterprise data technologies, including &lt;strong&gt;BISAM B-One, FactSet Performance, Snowflake, SQL, and Tableau&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mindset, intellectual curiosity, and a desire to continuously learn, experiment, and improve the way work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $190,000 – $220,000&amp;nbsp;per year. Actual compensation will be determined based on a candidate’s skills, qualifications, and relevant experience. In addition to base pay, this position may be eligible for discretionary incentive compensation&amp;nbsp;and includes participation in Acadian’s comprehensive benefits program, which includes health, retirement, and wellness offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To apply for this position or view Acadian’s open roles, please visit the Careers section of our website at:&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&quot;&gt; https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt; We will contact only selected candidates. &amp;nbsp;If you are a candidate with a disability, or are assisting a candidate with a disability, and require an accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, please email us at recruiting@acadian-asset.com.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Acadian Asset Management LLC is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all employees and&amp;nbsp; applicants. No employee or applicant shall be discriminated against on the basis of gender, race, creed, color, sex, age, national origin, marital status, pregnancy or parenthood, veteran status, citizenship status, disability, gender identity, or sexual orientation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

4868e575-3cdd-4aec-89a4-68754cd681e2:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acadian Asset Management is a global, systematic investment manager at the forefront of data-driven investing since 1986. Headquartered in Boston, with locations in Singapore, London, and Sydney, we manage over $232 billion on behalf of leading institutions worldwide—including pension funds, endowments, foundations, and sovereign wealth funds. We harness advanced technology, rich datasets, and multidisciplinary expertise to help clients navigate complex markets and uncover insights that may be overlooked by traditional approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What sets Acadian apart is our people. We foster a collaborative, intellectually curious environment where ideas are tested, diverse perspectives are welcomed, and innovation thrives. We’re united by a shared purpose: delivering effective client outcomes and supporting one another in work that’s both challenging and rewarding. We offer a flexible hybrid work environment, strong benefits, and a casual but focused office culture—all designed to support the meaningful, collaborative work that defines Acadian.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior AI Engineer is a senior technical leader responsible for defining, designing, and delivering enterprise-grade AI platforms and solutions across the firm. This role aligns diverse requirements and perspectives into coherent, scalable, and governable AI solutions.&amp;nbsp; The Senior AI Engineer sets technical standards, drives architectural consistency, and owns a slice of the firm-wide AI modernization and adoption roadmap, ensuring AI capabilities mature from experimentation to durable, production-grade systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acadian supports a hybrid work environment; employees are on-site in the Boston office 3 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns a slice of the firm’s AI architecture end-to-end, spanning agentic systems, software factories, knowledgebases, loops, custom harnesses, context and memory engineering, A2A, agentic deep research, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), LLM training, inference optimization, model integration, evaluations (evals).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with investment, engineering, sales, data, risk, security, and business teams to align diverse requirements into scalable and governable AI solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of production-grade AI systems, working alongside teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable and accelerate AI development within investment and research teams while ensuring alignment with enterprise architecture, controls, and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure AI solutions integrate cleanly with existing platforms, data sources, and workflows across the firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed governance, security, and risk controls into AI systems in collaboration with Risk, Compliance, and Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish approaches for model evaluation, monitoring, and lifecycle management appropriate for a regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously reassess and evolve AI architecture in response to new capabilities, risks, and firm priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and help shape shared AI platforms, tooling, and reusable components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption by ensuring AI solutions deliver measurable value to teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a technical mentor, leading through technical credibility, collaboration, and influence rather than formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Looking for Teammates With:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, engineering, physics, robotics, mathematics, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience with significant experience in senior or principal-level software engineering roles, with demonstrated ownership of complex, production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree or formal training in GenAI and Agents, machine learning, data science, or a related field is a plus, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing, building, and operating enterprise-grade AI or machine learning systems beyond prototypes and proofs of concept.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of modern AI architectures, including agentic systems, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), MCP, and LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to reason clearly about tradeoffs involving risk, cost, scalability, and time-to-value, and to communicate those decisions effectively to technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals, including API design, distributed systems, and cloud-native architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operationalizing AI systems, including testing, monitoring, evaluation, and lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively across highly skilled, opinionated teams, synthesizing diverse perspectives into aligned technical outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead through influence, collaboration, and technical credibility rather than formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud platforms and modern AI tooling ecosystems. Amazon Bedrock is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Risk, Compliance, Security, or Legal teams to embed controls into technical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with quantitative, research-driven, or investment-oriented AI use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regulated or highly risk-aware environments, such as financial services or asset management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad cross systems knowledge across AWS, K8s, software architecture, day 2 operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $175,000 – $225,000 per year. Actual compensation will be determined based on a candidate’s skills, qualifications, and relevant experience. In addition to base pay, this position may be eligible for discretionary incentive compensation and includes participation in Acadian’s comprehensive benefits program, which includes health, retirement, and wellness offerings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To apply for this position or view Acadian’s open roles, please visit the Careers section of our website at:&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&quot;&gt; https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt; We will contact only selected candidates. &amp;nbsp;If you are a candidate with a disability, or are assisting a candidate with a disability, and require an accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, please email us at recruiting@acadian-asset.com.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Acadian Asset Management LLC is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all employees and&amp;nbsp; applicants. No employee or applicant shall be discriminated against on the basis of gender, race, creed, color, sex, age, national origin, marital status, pregnancy or parenthood, veteran status, citizenship status, disability, gender identity, or sexual orientation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

341ac1c561438dc007f98735168bda017c7770e1:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a junior Execution Trader to support the trading procedures across equities, futures, and FX markets. The primary responsibility of this role is the accurate and timely execution of trading instructions while adhering to established processes, controls, and risk guidelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute trades across stocks, futures, and FX products in accordance with trading instructions and established procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor orders and execution outcomes to ensure accuracy and completeness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow operational workflows, risk controls, and compliance requirements with a high degree of diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records and assist with post-trade processes when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously seek to improve execution quality and operational efficiency while adhering to existing standards and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and a strong focus on accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to follow instructions carefully and execute tasks consistently without cutting corners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patient, methodical, and comfortable working within established processes and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership and accountability for completing assigned responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disciplined work ethic with the ability to remain focused during detail-intensive tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-oriented mindset with a willingness to support broader team objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Long-term commitment to developing expertise in execution and trading operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

8e4e5b05-f558-40c4-803f-d210ee072261:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acadian Asset Management is a global, systematic investment manager at the forefront of data-driven investing since 1986. Headquartered in Boston, with locations in Singapore, London, and Sydney, we manage over $232 billion on behalf of leading institutions worldwide—including pension funds, endowments, foundations, and sovereign wealth funds. We harness advanced technology, rich datasets, and multidisciplinary expertise to help clients navigate complex markets and uncover insights that may be overlooked by traditional approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What sets Acadian apart is our people. We foster a collaborative, intellectually curious environment where ideas are tested, diverse perspectives are welcomed, and innovation thrives. We’re united by a shared purpose: delivering effective client outcomes and supporting one another in work that’s both challenging and rewarding. We offer a flexible hybrid work environment, strong benefits, and a casual but focused office culture—all designed to support the meaningful, collaborative work that defines Acadian.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Architect is a key member of an IT Delivery Team supporting Acadian&#39;s Global Client Group, including Business Development, Client Service, Client Reporting, Marketing Production, RFP writing, and other business functions. Serving as a liaison between business stakeholders and Technology, the Senior Architect analyzes business processes, systems, and data to deliver scalable technology solutions and improve existing applications. The role partners closely with business users to understand objectives, streamline workflows, improve data quality, and reduce operational risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities span strategic initiatives, application enhancements, systems integration, and production support across business entity mastering, client reporting, client relationship and marketing technology, business intelligence, AI initiatives, and enterprise data platforms. The ideal candidate is a collaborative, analytical problem solver who thrives in a fast-paced environment, can manage competing priorities, and communicates effectively with both business and technical teams. This position reports to the Principal Business Analyst.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acadian supports a hybrid work environment; employees are on-site in the Boston office 3 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary liaison between business stakeholders and Technology to define and deliver effective solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships with business users to understand objectives, identify improvement opportunities, and translate requirements into actionable user stories and functional specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze business processes, systems, and data to improve efficiency, data quality, controls, and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document business workflows, functional requirements, acceptance criteria, business rules, and data governance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in solution design, testing, implementation, and post-production validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop test scenarios, coordinate user acceptance testing, and validate production releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate, prioritize, and coordinate resolution of production issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce clear documentation, knowledge articles, and user training materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other IT delivery teams on cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to product roadmaps and longer-term technology planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct meetings and drive collaboration between business and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Looking for Teammates With:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree required. MBA or CFA preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience as a Business Analyst, Business Systems Analyst or Business Architect in the investment management or investment software industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of investment management concepts, including clients, accounts, securities, cash flows, performance measurement, and client reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven knowledge in two or more of the following domains: Client Reporting, Investment Operations, Performance Measurement, Fund Accounting, CRM, Market Data, Trading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business, systems, and data analysis skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience gathering, documenting, and validating business and functional requirements in Agile environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate effectively with business and technical stakeholders, set priorities, and manage expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, organizational, problem-solving, written, and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, Python, or other data analysis tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with relational databases, APIs, JSON/XML, web services, and modern application architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data modeling and business intelligence tools (Tableau preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Salesforce, Seismic, SimCorp Coric, or similar CRM and client reporting platforms preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise master data platforms (account, security, position master) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AWS, AI technologies, and modern software development practices preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $175,000 – $200,000 per year. Actual compensation will be determined based on a candidate’s skills, qualifications, and relevant experience. In addition to base pay, this position may be eligible for discretionary incentive compensation and includes participation in Acadian’s comprehensive benefits program, which includes health, retirement, and wellness offerings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To apply for this position or view Acadian’s open roles, please visit the Careers section of our website at:&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&quot;&gt; https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt; We will contact only selected candidates. &amp;nbsp;If you are a candidate with a disability, or are assisting a candidate with a disability, and require an accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, please email us at recruiting@acadian-asset.com.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Acadian Asset Management LLC is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all employees and&amp;nbsp; applicants. No employee or applicant shall be discriminated against on the basis of gender, race, creed, color, sex, age, national origin, marital status, pregnancy or parenthood, veteran status, citizenship status, disability, gender identity, or sexual orientation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

01cd589f-6854-4f9a-b926-0ec4d1289779:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Acadian Asset Management is a global, systematic investment manager at the forefront of data-driven investing since 1986. Headquartered in Boston, with locations in Singapore, London, and Sydney, we manage over $232 billion on behalf of leading institutions worldwide—including pension funds, endowments, foundations, and sovereign wealth funds. We harness advanced technology, rich datasets, and multidisciplinary expertise to help clients navigate complex markets and uncover insights that may be overlooked by traditional approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What sets Acadian apart is our people. We foster a collaborative, intellectually curious environment where ideas are tested, diverse perspectives are welcomed, and innovation thrives. We’re united by a shared purpose: delivering effective client outcomes and supporting one another in work that’s both challenging and rewarding. We offer a flexible hybrid work environment, strong benefits, and a casual but focused office culture—all designed to support the meaningful, collaborative work that defines Acadian.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is in the Portfolio Control group within the Investment Operations department. The Portfolio Control team sits at the intersection of operations, fund accounting, and external service providers, with a focus on oversight, control, and issue resolution across client portfolios and Acadian funds. This role is responsible for ensuring the integrity of portfolio data, managing key operational relationships, and supporting the lifecycle of client accounts from onboarding through ongoing maintenance. In this role, you will gain exposure to a broad range of asset classes, global markets, and operational workflows, with opportunities to drive process improvements and interact with key internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Acadian supports a hybrid work environment; employees are on-site in the Boston office 3 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fund Oversight — Oversee portfolio accounting, custody, and middle-office functions. Investigate and resolve discrepancies across internal systems and external providers. Interact with custodians, prime brokers, and derivative counterparties (e.g., ISDA relationships) to support new fund launches, trading, collateral, and account maintenance activities. Reconcile proxy-voting reports and address inquiries from external and internal parties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New Account Startup/Onboarding — Prepare documentation to complete counterparty welcome packages for separately managed accounts, complete internal system setups, and act as a liaison between stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fund Administration — Manage and participate in oversight of fund expense processes including budgeting, accruals, invoice review, and payments. Prepare regulatory, compliance, and tax filings and support audits; research and resolve exceptions or breaches. Collaborate with external auditors and counterparties to finalize audited financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market Documentation — Open local markets for funds and maintain market and compliance documentation throughout the life of the fund.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax Reporting — Respond to client inquiries regarding fund taxes; facilitate K-1 and Canadian tax filings, Form 5500, PFIC and other tax reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Strategy — Identify process improvement opportunities including the use of AI across workflows, service providers, and systems; drive initiatives to enhance scalability, reduce operational risk, and improve data quality. Continuously assess and strengthen operational processes, controls, and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Skills – Advanced Excel proficiency; experience with portfolio accounting systems (e.g., Advent Geneva or similar) preferred. Experience with data analysis and visualization tools (e.g., Tableau) a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Looking for Teammates With:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Mathematics or Economics preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in investment operations, fund accounting, or related roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, interpersonal, and analytical skills with a proven ability to manage multiple priorities across daily tasks and long-term projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter; highly motivated and driven individual with a strong work ethic and integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, organizational, and interpersonal skills with a detail-oriented approach and a solid foundation in financial accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple priorities across daily tasks and long-term projects while effectively solving complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator with experience working cross-functionally and with external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to serve as a point of escalation for operational issues, driving root cause analysis and coordinating resolution across internal teams and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $105,000 – $125,000&amp;nbsp;per year. Actual compensation will be determined based on a candidate’s skills, qualifications, and relevant experience. In addition to base pay, this position may be eligible for discretionary incentive compensation&amp;nbsp;and includes participation in Acadian’s comprehensive benefits program, which includes health, retirement, and wellness offerings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To apply for this position or view Acadian’s open roles, please visit the Careers section of our website at:&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&quot;&gt; https://www.acadian-asset.com/careers/open-positions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;u&gt;.&lt;/u&gt; We will contact only selected candidates. &amp;nbsp;If you are a candidate with a disability, or are assisting a candidate with a disability, and require an accommodation to apply for one of our jobs, please email us at recruiting@acadian-asset.com.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Acadian Asset Management LLC is committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all employees and&amp;nbsp; applicants. No employee or applicant shall be discriminated against on the basis of gender, race, creed, color, sex, age, national origin, marital status, pregnancy or parenthood, veteran status, citizenship status, disability, gender identity, or sexual orientation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

500ba973ac6376bb371ab155e674b43df0104be3:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a global alternative investment management firm focused on pursuing outperformance for sophisticated clients via our Systematic, Discretionary and Solutions offerings. Powered by talent and advanced technology, our single and multi-manager investment strategies are underpinned by deep research and span public and private markets, across all major asset classes, with a significant focus on alternatives. Man Group takes a partnership approach to working with clients, establishing deep connections and creating tailored solutions to meet their investment goals and those of the millions of retirees and savers they represent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in London, we manage $253.6 billion* and operate across multiple offices globally. Man Group plc is listed on the London Stock Exchange under the ticker EMG.LN and is a constituent of the FTSE 250 Index. Further information can be found at &lt;a href=&quot;https://gbr01.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.man.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CSarah.Salta%40man.com%7C50106c0fbadc415bae6b08dd71e5d131%7Cf771e26b93bc4bbe8f6b7cd560ce9350%7C0%7C0%7C638791954087076774%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=5iuJXx8lcIhasW1cs1O9OyY6uKEhZDGiG5RgG9UVIsU%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.man.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-normal text-sm mb-4 last:mb-0 break-words&quot;&gt;At Man Group, we respect your privacy and we are committed to protecting and safeguarding your Personal Data. We have developed policies and processes which are designed to provide for the security and integrity of your Personal Data. We are committed to Processing your Personal Data fairly and lawfully, and being open and transparent about such Processing. For further information on how we process your data, please see the privacy notice for applicants&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;text-sm font-normal text-light-blue underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.man.com/privacy-notice-job-applicant&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;* As at 30 June 2026&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Purpose of the Role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Team Administrator supporting the Systematic investment teams, you will be the operational backbone for portfolio managers, the Client Portfolio Management team, and the broader Systematic business, working closely with colleagues in both Boston and London. No two days look the same. Your work will span calendar and travel management, client meeting logistics, materials preparation, and general office coordination, all in service of keeping a fast-moving investment team running smoothly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who thrives on variety, takes ownership of details large and small, and can move fluidly between independent tasks and close collaboration with sales, portfolio management, and administrative teams across Man&#39;s global offices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full administrative support to portfolio managers and investment teams as needed, including calendar management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating domestic and international business travel for portfolio managers and the wider Systematic team, including tickets, accommodation, taxi’s, visas, meetings and itineraries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Client Portfolio Management team; liaise with the global sales teams, organize client meetings and conference calls, booking conference rooms, catering, AV/ VC equipment if required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring the smooth running of the department on a daily basis, including monitoring the mailboxes, responding to requests, scheduling meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing remote cover for London.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collating meeting packs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onsite support for events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with local and regional administrative teams to ensure coordination across Man’s global business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with ad hoc projects as necessary, and providing cover for colleagues when needed, including printing and binding sales and marketing materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years in a similar administrative role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills with strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective collaborator and team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong time management skills; ability to handle multiple concurrent assignments, with a high degree of accuracy, and meet deadlines in a high pressure environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal and communication skills (both written and verbal)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High energy level and ability to perform in a fast paced environment under demanding conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient knowledge of MS Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint. Salesforce and Pardot experience is not required, but a plus (also Workday for expenses)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with travel booking and expense reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Windows, Excel, Word, and PowerPoint as well as databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The anticipated based salary range for this position is listed below. Compensation packages would also include benefits and a discretionary bonus. This is the base salary range that the Company believes it will pay for this position at the time of this posting based on the location and requirements of the position as well as the skills, qualifications, and experience of the applicant.&amp;nbsp; The Firm reserves the right to modify this pay range at any time.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Massachusetts Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$65,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$80,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion, Work-Life Balance and Benefits at Man Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll thrive in our working environment that champions equality of opportunity. Your unique perspective will contribute to our success, joining a workplace where inclusion is fundamental and deeply embedded in our culture and values. Through our external and internal initiatives, partnerships and programmes, you&#39;ll find opportunities to grow, develop your talents, and help foster an inclusive environment for all across our firm and industry. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.man.com/diversity&quot;&gt;www.man.com/diversity&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll have opportunities to make a difference through our charitable and global initiatives, while advancing your career through professional development, and with flexible working arrangements available too. Like all our people, you&#39;ll receive two annual &#39;Mankind&#39; days of paid leave for community volunteering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our comprehensive benefits package includes competitive holiday entitlements, pension/401k, life and long-term disability coverage, group sick pay, enhanced parental leave and long-service leave. Depending on your location, you may also enjoy additional benefits such as private medical coverage, discounted gym membership options and pet insurance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group provides equal employment opportunities to all applicants and all employees without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, ancestry, religion, disability, sex, gender identity and expression, marital status, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, age or any other legally protected category or status in accordance with applicable federal, state and local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Man Group is a Disability Confident Committed employer; if you require help or information on reasonable adjustments as you apply for roles with us, please contact&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:TalentAcquisition@man.com&quot;&gt;TalentAcquisition@man.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

0d14ef4f33f66b655585292210efba762aeb2bfc:
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital est une société renommée de négociation quantitative fondée en 1998. Tower a fondé ses affaires en se basant sur une plateforme à haute performance et sur des équipes de négociation indépendantes. Nous avons plus de 25 ans d’expérience en innovation et une réputation de découvrir des occasions uniques sur le marché.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower abrite certains des meilleurs talents mondiaux en matière de négociation systématique et d’ingénierie. Nous permettons aux gestionnaires de portefeuille de bâtir leurs équipes et leurs stratégies de façon indépendante tout en offrant les économies d’échelle qui proviennent d’une grande organisation mondiale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Les ingénieurs prospèrent chez Tower tout en développant une infrastructure de négociation électronique à un niveau de classe mondiale. Nos ingénieurs règlent des problèmes complexes dans les domaines de la programmation à faible latence, de la technologie FPGA, de l’accélération matérielle et de l’apprentissage automatique. Notre investissement continu dans les meilleurs talents d’ingénierie et dans les meilleures technologies garantit que notre plateforme demeure inégalée en termes de fonctionnalité, d’évolutivité et de performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;À Tower, chaque employé joue un rôle dans notre réussite. Nos équipes de soutien aux entreprises sont essentielles à la création et à la maintenance de la plateforme qui alimente toutes nos activités : elles réunissent l’accès au marché, les données, le calcul et l’infrastructure de recherche à la gestion des risques, la conformité et une gamme complète de services aux entreprises. Nos équipes de soutien aux entreprises permettent à nos équipes de négociation et d’ingénierie de donner le meilleur d’elles-mêmes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;À Tower, les employés trouveront un environnement stimulant et axé sur les résultats où des collègues très intelligents et motivés s’inspirent mutuellement pour atteindre leur plus grand potentiel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce poste s’inscrit dans le programme de rotation de Tower et offre une expérience pratique au sein de plusieurs équipes d’ingénierie. Grâce à des ateliers ciblés, à une formation structurée, à du mentorat et à des contributions directes aux systèmes de négociation en production, vous développerez une connaissance approfondie de notre architecture. Dans un délai de deux ans, ou plus tôt, vous intégrerez de façon permanente l’équipe qui correspond le mieux à vos compétences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Faire évoluer la plateforme de négociation afin de répondre aux besoins changeants de la recherche quantitative, de la simulation et de la négociation en production, en mettant particulièrement l’accent sur les données de marché et les systèmes d’exécution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer étroitement avec les chercheurs quantitatifs, les négociateurs et les ingénieurs logiciels pour concevoir, mettre en œuvre et déployer des stratégies de négociation systématique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concevoir et développer une infrastructure de négociation à haute performance permettant de recueillir les données de marché, de traiter les signaux de négociation et d’acheminer les ordres vers les différentes bourses mondiales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développer des cadres et des outils permettant aux chercheurs de créer rapidement des prototypes, d’effectuer des simulations rétrospectives, d’analyser et de déployer de nouvelles stratégies de négociation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développer des systèmes évolutifs offrant un accès efficace aux données de marché en temps réel et historiques à des fins de recherche, de simulation et de production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer avec les chercheurs afin de transformer les modèles quantitatifs en systèmes de production robustes et faciles à maintenir.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diriger les efforts de développement tout au long du cycle de vie des stratégies, depuis les outils de recherche et l’infrastructure de données jusqu’au déploiement et à la surveillance en production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimiser les systèmes de négociation et de recherche grâce à la conception de logiciels à faible latence, à la programmation réseau, à l’analyse des performances et à l’ingénierie des systèmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Créer des outils et des analyses permettant de repérer les tendances des marchés, d’évaluer le rendement des stratégies et d’améliorer les décisions de négociation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développer des systèmes de gestion des risques, de surveillance et d’attribution de la performance destinés aux chercheurs et aux négociateurs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyser le comportement des systèmes de négociation en production et collaborer avec les équipes responsables des stratégies afin de diagnostiquer les problèmes liés à la performance, à l’exécution et aux données de marché.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer à l’architecture de plateformes communes visant à améliorer la productivité des équipes de recherche, de développement et de négociation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diplôme en informatique, en génie, en mathématiques, en physique ou dans un domaine technique connexe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;De 0 à 2 ans d’expérience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solides connaissances des algorithmes, des structures de données, des systèmes distribués et de la conception logicielle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellentes compétences en programmation C++; une expérience en Python est fortement souhaitée.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intérêt pour les marchés financiers, la négociation systématique et les processus de recherche quantitative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience dans le développement de systèmes à haute performance, d’applications à forte intensité de données ou de logiciels à faible latence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à collaborer efficacement avec des chercheurs quantitatifs, des négociateurs et des ingénieurs afin de résoudre des problèmes techniques et analytiques complexes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solides capacités d’analyse et de résolution de problèmes, avec un souci constant d’exactitude et de performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacité à gérer plusieurs projets et priorités dans un environnement au rythme soutenu.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellentes aptitudes en communication et esprit de collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre siège social de Tower est situé dans l’édifice Équitable, au plein cœur du district financier de New York. Toutefois, notre influence est mondiale, et nous avons plus d’une douzaine de bureaux dans le monde entier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;À Tower, nous croyons que le travail devrait être à la fois stimulant et agréable. C’est pourquoi nous favorisons une culture où les personnes intelligentes et motivées prospèrent, sans les egos. Notre milieu de travail à concept ouvert, notre code vestimentaire décontracté et nos cuisines bien approvisionnées reflètent la valeur que nous accordons à un environnement amical et collaboratif où tout le monde est respecté et où les bonnes idées sont gagnantes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nos avantages comprennent :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Politiques généreuses de congés payés&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Régimes d’épargne et autres outils de bien-être financier disponibles dans chaque région&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasions de travail hybride&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Déjeuner, dîner et collations gratuits quotidiennement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expériences de bien-être au bureau et remboursement de certaines dépenses de bien-être (p. ex., centre de conditionnement physique, entraînement personnel et plus encore)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasions de bénévolat et dons de charité&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Événements sociaux, cinq à sept, friandises et célébrations tout au long de l’année&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ateliers et occasions d’apprentissage continu&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;À Tower, vous trouverez une culture collaborative et accueillante, une équipe diversifiée et un milieu de travail qui valorise à la fois le rendement et le plaisir. Pas de hiérarchie inutile. Pas d’ego. Juste des gens formidables qui font un travail formidable, ensemble.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital est un employeur qui souscrit au principe de l’égalité d’accès à l’emploi.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;***&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is a leading quantitative trading firm founded in 1998. Tower has built its business on a high-performance platform and independent trading teams. We have a 25+ year track record of innovation and a reputation for discovering unique market opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is part of Tower’s rotational program, offering hands-on experience across multiple engineering teams. Through targeted workshops, structured training, mentorship, and direct contributions to production trading systems, you will build deep expertise in our architecture. Within two years, or sooner, you will transition into a permanent placement on a team that best matches your skill sets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the trading platform to support the changing needs of quantitative research, simulation, and production trading, with particular emphasis on market data and execution systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with quantitative researchers, traders, and software engineers to design, implement, and deploy systematic trading strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop high-performance trading infrastructure responsible for collecting market data, processing trading signals, and routing orders to exchanges around the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build frameworks and tools that enable researchers to rapidly prototype, backtest, analyze, and deploy new trading strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable systems that provide efficient access to live and historical market data for research, simulation, and production use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with researchers to translate quantitative models into robust, maintainable production systems. Lead development efforts across the strategy lifecycle, from research tooling and data infrastructure to production deployment and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize trading and research systems through low-latency software design, network programming, performance analysis, and systems-level engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create tools and analytics that help identify market patterns, evaluate strategy performance, and improve trading decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build risk management, monitoring, and performance attribution systems used by researchers and traders. Investigate production trading behavior and partner with strategy teams to diagnose performance, execution, and market data issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the architecture of shared platforms that improve productivity across research, development, and trading teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or a related technical field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-2 years of experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in algorithms, data structures, distributed systems, and software design.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent programming skills in C++, with experience in Python strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in financial markets, systematic trading, and quantitative research workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building high-performance systems, data-intensive applications, or low-latency software. The ability to collaborate effectively with quantitative researchers, traders, and engineers to solve complex technical and analytical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities with a focus on both correctness and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable managing multiple projects and priorities in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and a collaborative mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

